- &lt;i&gt;P&lt;/i&gt;.

00:13:45.222 --> 00:13:46.872
- Yes, &lt;i&gt;P&lt;/i&gt;.

00:13:46.957 --> 00:13:48.169
- Ну, &lt;i&gt;Р&lt;/i&gt; українська.

00:13:48.254 --> 00:13:49.377
- Bravo! &lt;i&gt;P&lt;/i&gt;.

00:13:49.462 --> 00:13:50.336
- &lt;i&gt;N&lt;/i&gt;?

00:13:50.421 --> 00:13:51.429
- Yes.

00:13:52.500 --> 00:13:53.770
- &lt;i&gt;E&lt;/i&gt;.

00:13:53.865 --> 00:13:58.888
- Yes! And the score is
one-one. It’s a plane! Amazing!

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:01.664
- So, we don’t have a winner.

00:14:01.749 --> 00:14:04.992
When there is one-one,
we say “&lt;i&gt;дружба&lt;/i&gt;”, yes?

00:14:05.077 --> 00:14:06.841
So, in English this is &lt;i&gt;draw&lt;/i&gt;.

00:14:07.335 --> 00:14:08.383
- &lt;i&gt;Draw&lt;/i&gt;? A &lt;i&gt;draw&lt;/i&gt;.

00:14:08.468 --> 00:14:09.476
- Like &lt;i&gt;bro&lt;/i&gt;?

00:14:09.801 --> 00:14:11.715
- Or a &lt;i&gt;tie&lt;/i&gt; – як краватка.

00:14:11.800 --> 00:14:12.661
- &lt;i&gt;Draw.&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:12.746 --> 00:14:14.137
- &lt;i&gt;Draw&lt;/i&gt; or a &lt;i&gt;tie&lt;/i&gt;.

00:14:14.294 --> 00:14:15.302
It’s nice.

00:14:15.921 --> 00:14:20.924
So, if we have a look at
these transports, let’s discuss,

00:14:21.009 --> 00:14:26.214
which transport is fast
and which one is slow.

00:14:27.025 --> 00:14:30.750
- But you need to tell me, you
need to give me a sentence.

00:14:30.835 --> 00:14:35.643
For example: I think taxi is slow.

00:14:35.728 --> 00:14:36.697
Or fast.

00:14:36.782 --> 00:14:37.643
Okay?

00:14:37.728 --> 00:14:39.351
Give me the full sentence.

00:14:40.032 --> 00:14:41.722
So, who wants to start?

00:14:43.694 --> 00:14:46.056
We’ll start with start and slow first.

00:14:46.349 --> 00:14:48.207
Fast and slow.

00:14:48.302 --> 00:14:49.496
- Сan? Yes please.

00:14:49.581 --> 00:14:54.786
- I think that helicopter
is a fast transport.

00:14:54.992 --> 00:14:58.880
- It’s fast, okay. Is it the fastest?

00:15:00.654 --> 00:15:06.925
- In some point, when we are
in the mountains – yes. For sure.

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:10.483
- Aha, okay, so you
think that helicopter is fast.

00:15:10.595 --> 00:15:13.246
Alex, what about you? What do you think?

00:15:13.563 --> 00:15:15.793
- I think plane is fast.

00:15:15.878 --> 00:15:18.063
- Okay, good.

00:15:19.729 --> 00:15:23.040
- What is slow? What do
you think is the slowest?

00:15:23.905 --> 00:15:25.346
- Tram?

00:15:25.872 --> 00:15:27.853
- The tram is the slowest?

00:15:28.341 --> 00:15:29.349
- Can be.

00:15:29.434 --> 00:15:32.421
- Can be. Depends on the situation.

00:15:32.548 --> 00:15:34.383
- Or a ship?

00:15:34.468 --> 00:15:37.733
- Ship can be quite slow as
well when they are cruising.

00:15:37.818 --> 00:15:39.590
- Or a bus if we are having a…

00:15:39.675 --> 00:15:40.683
- Traffic jam?

00:15:40.768 --> 00:15:41.979
- Traffic jam, yeah.

00:15:42.064 --> 00:15:43.342
- Oh, okay, well.

00:15:43.427 --> 00:15:48.977
I think, when there is a traffic jam
every single mean of transport is so slow.

00:15:49.062 --> 00:15:51.078
- But not the helicopter or plane!

00:15:51.163 --> 00:15:52.902
- Yeah, so it’s prioritizing.

00:15:52.987 --> 00:15:54.522
- Or a motorcycle.

00:15:54.607 --> 00:15:56.479
- Motorcycle is also possible.

00:15:56.564 --> 00:16:00.180
But the best one for traffic
jam is bicycle, I guess. Agree?

00:16:00.265 --> 00:16:02.574
- But we don’t have it here.

00:16:02.762 --> 00:16:05.119
- So, exciting or boring.

00:16:05.309 --> 00:16:07.134
Exciting? Or boring?

00:16:07.219 --> 00:16:09.856
So, let’s discuss this
thing, these criteria.

00:16:13.377 --> 00:16:14.443
- Alina?

00:16:15.079 --> 00:16:19.524
- I can say that the
train is exciting for me.

00:16:19.610 --> 00:16:23.384
Because I like to read or watch something.

00:16:23.469 --> 00:16:26.975
- Okay, what do you usually
do on the train when you travel?

00:16:27.060 --> 00:16:28.496
Apart from reading.

00:16:29.371 --> 00:16:31.090
- I read some books.

00:16:31.175 --> 00:16:32.210
- Okay.

00:16:32.303 --> 00:16:35.471
- I like to read books
or to drink classic tea.

00:16:35.587 --> 00:16:36.643
- Okay.

00:16:36.728 --> 00:16:38.800
- In Ukrainian train.

00:16:38.885 --> 00:16:41.341
- It’s the Ukrainian tea.

00:16:41.444 --> 00:16:47.298
- I love Ukrainian train, tea. It’s
like the classic thing, tradition.

00:16:47.452 --> 00:16:48.460
- Perfect.

00:16:48.545 --> 00:16:49.830
- With some sweets.

00:16:50.286 --> 00:16:54.210
- So, this is like a habit
for you. A part of a routine.

00:16:54.295 --> 00:17:01.253
- To get from Kyiv to my land – it’s
like 16 hours. So, I'm enjoying the time.

00:17:01.338 --> 00:17:04.381
- Yes, I understand this.
What about you, Alex?

00:17:04.690 --> 00:17:06.699
- Так, значить я…

00:17:06.784 --> 00:17:08.042
- Exciting or boring?

00:17:08.127 --> 00:17:11.645
- Boring – tram. Буду
настоювати на своєму.

00:17:12.348 --> 00:17:16.336
- Why do you think that tram is
boring? It’s not interesting at all?

00:17:16.421 --> 00:17:19.357
- You’ve never been in a party-tram.

00:17:19.659 --> 00:17:20.667
- No.

00:17:21.167 --> 00:17:26.396
- Party-tram is nice, I guess it can
be. And we also can have a party-bus.

00:17:26.481 --> 00:17:27.317
- Yeah.

00:17:27.413 --> 00:17:29.967
- We can have a party-bus as well. Okay.

00:17:30.119 --> 00:17:32.262
Relaxing or tiring.

00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:34.367
So, relaxing trip.

00:17:34.452 --> 00:17:38.571
This is – you enjoy your trip, you
leave the transport very relaxed

00:17:38.656 --> 00:17:40.588
or tiring, exhausting.

00:17:40.673 --> 00:17:42.353
You don’t have any feelings.

00:17:42.438 --> 00:17:43.730
- So, can I answer?

00:17:43.815 --> 00:17:45.011
- Yes, Alina.

00:17:45.183 --> 00:17:51.371
- I didn’t use so much the
ship to go somewhere very far.

00:17:51.456 --> 00:17:54.579
But plane, for sure, yes.

00:17:54.730 --> 00:18:00.520
And it’s tiring for me because
it’s really like all these moments.

00:18:00.605 --> 00:18:02.793
To give your documents, after – wait.

00:18:02.878 --> 00:18:04.579
After – do that and that.

00:18:04.664 --> 00:18:08.602
Yeah, so it’s tiring for
me but it’s really fast

00:18:08.687 --> 00:18:12.236
because you can get to another country.

00:18:12.321 --> 00:18:16.807
- And sometimes this is the only possible
connection – with the plane. Right?

00:18:16.892 --> 00:18:18.079
- Yeah, right.

00:18:18.164 --> 00:18:21.988
- And this can also be very tiring
if you have a connection flight

00:18:22.073 --> 00:18:25.271
and you need to stay in
the airport and wait, and wait.

00:18:25.356 --> 00:18:27.200
- Yeah, I got a lot of stories.

00:18:27.285 --> 00:18:30.841
- What about you, Alex?
What’s for you relaxing or tiring?

00:18:30.943 --> 00:18:32.372
- Tiring – it’s tram.

00:18:32.476 --> 00:18:34.963
- Tram is your favourite.

00:18:35.048 --> 00:18:35.995
- Yeah.

00:18:36.080 --> 00:18:39.497
- Do you remember the
last day you were on a tram?

00:18:39.582 --> 00:18:40.494
- Never.

00:18:40.579 --> 00:18:43.046
- You definitely need to try it.

00:18:43.698 --> 00:18:44.991
- I hate tram.

00:18:45.103 --> 00:18:50.166
- You hate trams? It’s a pity.
This can be nice.

00:18:50.524 --> 00:18:54.214
- We’re gonna get him to Podil party-tram.

00:18:54.299 --> 00:18:57.192
- Okay, so let’s schedule the meeting.

00:18:57.277 --> 00:18:58.453
Okay.

00:18:58.538 --> 00:19:03.808
Now, let’s have a look at this
transport in terms of cheap or expensive.

00:19:03.893 --> 00:19:05.722
And let’s rank.

00:19:06.214 --> 00:19:10.111
Rank means that number one is the cheapest

00:19:10.337 --> 00:19:13.786
and number eight, because we
have eight means of transport,

00:19:13.871 --> 00:19:15.817
is the most expensive one.

00:19:15.928 --> 00:19:17.219
Okay? - Okay.

00:19:17.325 --> 00:19:19.279
